alice: quick check — noticed error spikes on staging when rotating db creds via ExternalSecrets. PR applied but pods keep restarting, appears like secret re-creation loop after we changed the template annotations. anyone seen this?

ben: saw it earlier. controller reconciled and created a new k8s secret with different metadata which triggered a rollout. suspect the TF change set `metadata.annotations = null` for the template.

alice: linking PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/4321 — helm values changed for external-secrets chart, we toggled the mapTemplate to include annotations.

cara: if annotations/metadata change, kube treats secret as a new object and projected volumes can flip inodes -> sidecars restart. we should avoid blowing away metadata. quick check: `kubectl describe secret payments-db-staging -n staging` to see the annotation diffs.

ben: minimal repro from controller logs: it overwrote `annotations: { 'secrets.redwood/rotated-at': null }` because template had nulls. we should set explicit values or remove the key entirely. example controller log snippet: ```json
{"msg":"reconciled secret","name":"payments-db-staging","annotations":{"secrets.redwood/rotated-at":null}}
```

david: quick TF patch suggestion (will open tiny PR): ```hcl
resource "kubernetes_external_secret" "payments" {
  template = {
    metadata = {
      annotations = {
        "secrets.redwood/rotated-at" = "${timestamp()}"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

alice: so change is to avoid `null` and use a timestamp label instead or remove annotation entirely. can someone lgtm the infra PR? it's a small cleanup + add `reconcileStrategy = "merge"` to the ExternalSecret. :pray:

ben: LGTM from infra. also recommend adding a post-rotation smoke check in the canary job: `kubectl exec -n staging $POD -- curl -sfS localhost:8080/health` and validate env var for DB connection. i'll add that to the canary pipeline.

